      "text": "[中文](docs/README.zh.md)\n\n`dsh-team-bots` is a DSH plugin that turns one workspace into a team: project group chats, a task board, write-scope parallel scheduling, shared memory and skills, approval cards, usage and cost, and a personal WeChat channel. Every run keeps its trajectory, duration, token count and cost."
    },
    {
      "section": "Requirements",
      "text": "- Node.js ≥ 22.19\n- the DSH CLI (`dsh`)\n\nThe plugin runs inside the DSH Web process. It has no standalone service and no port of its own."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install",
      "text": "```sh\ndsh plugin --profile <name> add dsh-team-bots\n```\n\nFrom a checkout (packs the working tree and installs it into the profile):\n\n```sh\nnpm run profile:install -- --profile <name>\n```\n\nPlugin files inside a profile are a snapshot. After changing code, reinstall — otherwise the page keeps serving the old build."
    },
    {
      "section": "Open the workspace",
      "text": "```text\nhttp://<host>:<port>/                     DSH web, auto-login into the team workspace\nhttp://<host>:<port>/api/dsh-team/ui      the team workspace itself\n```\n\nThe first visit exchanges the current startup token for a 30-day login cookie. Auto-login means anyone who can reach the port becomes owner, so listen on the local machine or a trusted network; for public use put an HTTPS reverse proxy in front that forwards Host and WebSocket correctly."
    },
    {
      "section": "Group chats and dispatch",
      "text": "Every project is a group chat. A bot can also be addressed one-to-one in a dispatch view. Session bindings run in four lanes — task, solo, dm, project — so a group chat, a task run and a direct message never block each other."
    },
    {
      "section": "Task board",
      "text": "States: backlog, todo, in progress, blocked, in review, done, canceled. A card carries assignee, priority, parent/child links, tags, write scopes, an optional time budget (a hard limit that aborts the run), comments, and its own usage. Rows are grouped by state and can be dragged onto another group to change status."
    },
    {
      "section": "Write scopes and parallel scheduling",
      "text": "A card declares the paths it will write, relative to the project working directory. Two runs of the same project run in parallel only when both declare scopes and the path prefixes do not overlap; a card with no declared scope is treated as serial. An urgent card may be exempted from the queue — the exemption is written into the card's creation message rather than applied silently."
    },
    {
      "section": "Memory, skills, evolution proposals",
      "text": "Memory entries are written, reviewed, frozen and archived by the owner, and are readable by every bot in the project. Skills come from a shared skill root plus per-project skills; changing them goes through a proposal, an approval and an apply, with a canary stage before promotion to full effect. The same path can change a bot's role instructions."
    },
    {
      "section": "Approval and question cards",
      "text": "When a bot asks for a tool approval, a secret, or an answer, the workspace shows a card in the chat. The owner approves, denies or answers in place, and the decision is recorded on the card."
    },
    {
      "section": "Usage and cost",
      "text": "The usage page breaks the numbers down by model, bot and project, exports CSV, and reads model prices from configuration. Run limits (timeout abort, no-progress watchdog, review idle threshold) and budgets are set per workspace."
    },
    {
      "section": "Terminal, channels, secrets",
      "text": "A per-project terminal runs commands in the project directory. The WeChat channel binds by QR code and pushes task activity to the owner's WeChat. Secrets are scoped to the team or to one project; values are only ever shown as a fingerprint and are handed out as one-time runtime copies that expire."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Variable | Default | Meaning |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `DSH_TEAM_WORKSPACE` | `~/.dsh/workspace/team-bots` | team workspace root |\n| `DSH_TEAM_DATA` | `<workspace>/.data` | database and run records |\n\nEvery other variable, its default, and its resolution order (explicit env > value saved in the workspace > code default) live in `src/config.ts`; `.env.example` lists the common ones. Do not put a `.env` file in the repository root — it would leak `DSH_*` into `npm test` and `npm run dev`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "`DSH_TEAM_DATA` holds `team.sqlite`, `wechat-channel.sqlite`, `secret.key`, `memory/`, `messages/` and `secrets-runtime/`. Back up `secret.key` together with the data: without it the stored ciphertext cannot be decrypted."
